   1:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c **** /**
   2:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****   ******************************************************************************
   3:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****   * @file    stm32f4xx_dma.c
   4:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****   * @author  MCD Application Team
   5:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****   * @version V1.8.0
   6:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****   * @date    04-November-2016
   7:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****   * @brief   This file provides firmware functions to manage the following 
   8:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****   *          functionalities of the Direct Memory Access controller (DMA):           
   9:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****   *           + Initialization and Configuration
  10:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****   *           + Data Counter
  11:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****   *           + Double Buffer mode configuration and command  
  12:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****   *           + Interrupts and flags management
  13:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****   *           
  14:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****   @verbatim      
  15:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****  ===============================================================================      
  16:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****                        ##### How to use this driver #####
  17:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****  ===============================================================================
  18:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****     [..] 
  19:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****       (#) Enable The DMA controller clock using RCC_AHB1PeriphResetCmd(RCC_AHB1Periph_DMA1, ENABLE)
  20:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           function for DMA1 or using RCC_AHB1PeriphResetCmd(RCC_AHB1Periph_DMA2, ENABLE)
  21:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           function for DMA2.
  22:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****   
  23:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****       (#) Enable and configure the peripheral to be connected to the DMA Stream
  24:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           (except for internal SRAM / FLASH memories: no initialization is 
  25:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           necessary). 
  26:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           
  27:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****       (#) For a given Stream, program the required configuration through following parameters:   
  28:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           Source and Destination addresses, Transfer Direction, Transfer size, Source and Destinati
  29:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           data formats, Circular or Normal mode, Stream Priority level, Source and Destination 
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccx7iGzk.s 			page 2


  30:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           Incrementation mode, FIFO mode and its Threshold (if needed), Burst 
  31:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           mode for Source and/or Destination (if needed) using the DMA_Init() function.
  32:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           To avoid filling unnecessary fields, you can call DMA_StructInit() function
  33:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           to initialize a given structure with default values (reset values), the modify
  34:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           only necessary fields 
  35:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           (ie. Source and Destination addresses, Transfer size and Data Formats).
  36:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****   
  37:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****       (#) Enable the NVIC and the corresponding interrupt(s) using the function 
  38:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           DMA_ITConfig() if you need to use DMA interrupts. 
  39:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****   
  40:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****       (#) Optionally, if the Circular mode is enabled, you can use the Double buffer mode by config
  41:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           the second Memory address and the first Memory to be used through the function 
  42:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           DMA_DoubleBufferModeConfig(). Then enable the Double buffer mode through the function
  43:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           DMA_DoubleBufferModeCmd(). These operations must be done before step 6.
  44:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****       
  45:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****       (#) Enable the DMA stream using the DMA_Cmd() function. 
  46:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****                   
  47:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****       (#) Activate the needed Stream Request using PPP_DMACmd() function for
  48:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           any PPP peripheral except internal SRAM and FLASH (ie. SPI, USART ...)
  49:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           The function allowing this operation is provided in each PPP peripheral
  50:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           driver (ie. SPI_DMACmd for SPI peripheral).
  51:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           Once the Stream is enabled, it is not possible to modify its configuration
  52:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           unless the stream is stopped and disabled.
  53:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           After enabling the Stream, it is advised to monitor the EN bit status using
  54:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           the function DMA_GetCmdStatus(). In case of configuration errors or bus errors
  55:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           this bit will remain reset and all transfers on this Stream will remain on hold.      
  56:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****   
  57:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****       (#) Optionally, you can configure the number of data to be transferred
  58:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           when the Stream is disabled (ie. after each Transfer Complete event
  59:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           or when a Transfer Error occurs) using the function DMA_SetCurrDataCounter().
  60:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           And you can get the number of remaining data to be transferred using 
  61:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           the function DMA_GetCurrDataCounter() at run time (when the DMA Stream is
  62:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           enabled and running).  
  63:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****                      
  64:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****       (#) To control DMA events you can use one of the following two methods:
  65:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****         (##) Check on DMA Stream flags using the function DMA_GetFlagStatus().  
  66:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****         (##) Use DMA interrupts through the function DMA_ITConfig() at initialization
  67:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****              phase and DMA_GetITStatus() function into interrupt routines in
  68:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****              communication phase.
  69:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****     [..]     
  70:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           After checking on a flag you should clear it using DMA_ClearFlag()
  71:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           function. And after checking on an interrupt event you should 
  72:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           clear it using DMA_ClearITPendingBit() function.    
  73:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****                 
  74:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****       (#) Optionally, if Circular mode and Double Buffer mode are enabled, you can modify
  75:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           the Memory Addresses using the function DMA_MemoryTargetConfig(). Make sure that
  76:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           the Memory Address to be modified is not the one currently in use by DMA Stream.
  77:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           This condition can be monitored using the function DMA_GetCurrentMemoryTarget().
  78:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****                 
  79:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****       (#) Optionally, Pause-Resume operations may be performed:
  80:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           The DMA_Cmd() function may be used to perform Pause-Resume operation. 
  81:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           When a transfer is ongoing, calling this function to disable the 
  82:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           Stream will cause the transfer to be paused. All configuration registers 
  83:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           and the number of remaining data will be preserved. When calling again 
  84:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           this function to re-enable the Stream, the transfer will be resumed from 
  85:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****           the point where it was paused.          
  86:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****                    
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccx7iGzk.s 			page 3


  87:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****       -@- Memory-to-Memory transfer is possible by setting the address of the memory into
  88:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****            the Peripheral registers. In this mode, Circular mode and Double Buffer mode
  89:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****            are not allowed.
  90:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****     
  91:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****       -@- The FIFO is used mainly to reduce bus usage and to allow data 
  92:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****            packing/unpacking: it is possible to set different Data Sizes for 
  93:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****            the Peripheral and the Memory (ie. you can set Half-Word data size 
  94:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****            for the peripheral to access its data register and set Word data size
  95:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****            for the Memory to gain in access time. Each two Half-words will be 
  96:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****            packed and written in a single access to a Word in the Memory).
  97:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****       
  98:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****       -@- When FIFO is disabled, it is not allowed to configure different 
  99:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****            Data Sizes for Source and Destination. In this case the Peripheral 
 100:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****            Data Size will be applied to both Source and Destination.               
 101:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****   
 102:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****   @endverbatim
 103:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dma.c ****   ******************************************************************************
